-    "content": "# [Informational] Role and Permission Matrix\n\nThis document defines the authoritative, fine-grained access control model across all 7 principal tiers in the \ud83d\udc4dkanban platform.\n\nThe platform enforces Row-Level Security (FORCE RLS) at the PostgreSQL database layer, capability bitmasks with explicit DENY precedence, multi-factor AAL2 step-up authentication, and strict cryptographic scoping for agents and custom scripts.\n\n---\n\n## Legend\n\n| Symbol | Status | Description |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **\u25cf** | **Allowed by Role** | Operation is natively permitted by the principal tier without extra elevation. |\n| **\u25d0** | **Conditional** | Operation requires an explicit ACL share, matching token scope, project assignment, or fresh AAL2 step-up verification. |\n| **\u25cb** | **Never Allowed** | Operation is strictly forbidden by policy and rejected by database RLS or API gatekeepers. |\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"system-roles\"></a>\n## The 7 Principal Tiers\n\n1. **Guest (`WORKSPACE_GUEST` / `PROJECT_GUEST`):** Ephemeral or external collaborator. Confined strictly to explicitly shared objects with zero ambient project or workspace visibility.\n2. **Viewer (`WORKSPACE_VIEWER` / `PROJECT_VIEWER`):** Read-only stakeholder. Permitted to inspect un-restricted workspace or project assets, but cannot author or modify data.\n3. **Member (`WORKSPACE_MEMBER` / `PROJECT_MEMBER`):** Standard day-to-day engineer or contributor. Can author and manage issues, docs, stickies, and views in assigned projects.\n4. **Project Admin (`PROJECT_ADMIN`):** Lead for a specific project. Controls project configuration, workflow state transitions, WIP limits, project member bindings, and project trash.\n5. **Workspace Admin (`WORKSPACE_ADMIN`):** Organization administrator. Governs workspace settings, groups, user provisioning, retention policy, and workspace trash studio.\n6. **Server Admin (`SERVER_ADMIN`):** Root platform operator. Manages global server topology, multi-card authentication, air-gap flags, and cryptographic permanent purge.\n7. **Scoped MCP Agent (Service Principal):** Autonomous or assisted agent accessing `/mcp/agent`, `/mcp/docs`, or `/mcp/admin` bound to an API key or OAuth 2.0 PKCE token.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"workspace-level-roles\"></a>\n## Master Capability Matrix\n\n| Operational Capability | Guest | Viewer | Member | Project Admin | Workspace Admin | Server Admin | Scoped MCP Agent |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **Viewing Workspace-Public Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Viewing Private Project Objects** | \u25d0 (2) | \u25d0 (2) | \u25d0 (2) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 2) |\n| **Explicit ACL DENY Precedence** | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) |\n| **Authoring Issues, Stickies, and Docs** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Editing and Versioning Pages** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Managing Resource ACLs (Share / Revoke)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (4) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 4) |\n| **Project Studio and Workflow Management** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Custom Field and Script Definition** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (5) | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 5) |\n| **Soft-Trash Project Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (6) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 6) |\n| **Workspace Trash Studio Inspection** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (7) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1, 8) |\n| **Restoring Soft-Deleted Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (7) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1, 8) |\n| **Workspace Retention Policy (7 to 365 Days)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Automated Multi-Object Sweep (trash_purge)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (9) | \u25cb |\n| **2-Stage Permanent Purge (Cryptographic)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8, 10) | \u25cb |\n| **Local User Provisioning and Password Reset** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Role Bindings and Group Hierarchy CRUD** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (11) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Multi-Card Auth Studio and Passkey Config** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Minting Scoped MCP API Keys** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Immutable Audit Ledger (Inspection Only)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Tampering with Audit Ledger Records** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb (12) | \u25cb |\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Condition Notes\n\n1. **Token Scope Restriction:** Scoped MCP Agents can only exercise capabilities explicitly included in their minted token scopes (`read:issues`, `write:issues`, `read:docs`, `write:docs`, `admin`, etc.). Unscoped tools are rejected with `403 FORBIDDEN`.\n2. **Explicit Project Membership / ACL Share:** Guests and Viewers cannot see private project entities unless explicitly added to the project role bindings or granted a specific `ALLOW` entry in `resource_acl_entries`.\n3. **Absolute DENY Precedence:** If an explicit `DENY` entry exists for a principal on an object (or inherited group), effective capability bitmasks collapse immediately (`allow & (~deny)`). Even Workspace Admins cannot view or manage objects guarded by an explicit `DENY`.\n4. **Ownership Share Delegation:** Standard Members can only share objects they originally authored, provided project policy permits user-level ACL delegation.\n5. **Admin Approval Gate:** Custom fields and scripts can only be defined by administrators. Executing a script with Workspace or Server token escalation requires cryptographic approval from an administrator of that tier.\n6. **Author Deletion Scope:** Members may soft-delete their own drafts, comments, and un-assigned stickies if granted DELETE capability mask. Project-wide item soft-deletion requires Project Admin.\n7. **Project Scope Isolation:** Project Admins in the Trash Studio can only view and restore items belonging to projects where they hold explicit `PROJECT_ADMIN` authority.\n8. **Fresh AAL2 Step-Up Requirement:** All administrative endpoints (`/api/v1/admin/*`, retention settings, user provisioning, trash operations, key minting) enforce `Depends(require_admin_aal2)`. The session must have verified MFA within the last 900 seconds (`aal2_verified_at <= 900s`).\n9. **Daemon Background Job Authority:** The trash purge runner executes with dedicated system worker identity and sweeps expired entities strictly past their per-workspace `trash_retention_days` threshold.\n10. **2-Stage Destructive Confirmation:** Permanent purge is exclusively gated to `SERVER_ADMIN` + fresh AAL2. It requires `POST /api/v1/admin/destructive:request` to compute blast radius and mint an ephemeral HMAC `confirmation_token` + `blast_hash`, followed by `POST /api/v1/admin/destructive:execute` with a mandatory human reason (10 to 500 characters).\n11. **Project-Level Role Delegation:** Project Admins may manage role bindings within their designated project only. They cannot elevate users to Workspace Admin or Server Admin.\n12. **Cryptographic Immutability:** Audit ledger tables (`activity_ledger`) have no `UPDATE` or `DELETE` grants for any database role (including `kanban_app` and `kanban_migrator`). Triggers prevent tampering.\n\n---\n\n## Architectural Security Invariants\n\n- **Hostile Wire Invariant:** Every input is validated with strict Pydantic schemas and UTF-8 surrogate checks. Cleartext transmission of tokens is prohibited.\n- **Walled Component Garden:** Row-Level Security (`FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`) is always active on all database sessions. Dropping session authorization to unprivileged users is mandatory in application flows.\n- **Volatile State Sanitization:** Ephemeral tokens and secrets exist only in memory during execution and are erased immediately after verification.\n- **Supply Chain Paranoia:** Zero external cloud runtime dependencies for core authentication, authorization, or search.\n"
+    "content": "# [Informational] Role and Permission Matrix\n\nThis document defines the authoritative, fine-grained access control model across all 7 principal tiers in the \ud83d\udc4dkanban platform.\n\nThe platform enforces Row-Level Security (FORCE RLS) at the PostgreSQL database layer, capability bitmasks with explicit DENY precedence, multi-factor AAL2 step-up authentication, and strict cryptographic scoping for agents and custom scripts.\n\n---\n\n## Legend\n\n| Symbol | Status | Description |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| **\u25cf** | **Allowed by Role** | Operation is natively permitted by the principal tier without extra elevation. |\n| **\u25d0** | **Conditional** | Operation requires an explicit ACL share, matching token scope, project assignment, or fresh AAL2 step-up verification. |\n| **\u25cb** | **Never Allowed** | Operation is strictly forbidden by policy and rejected by database RLS or API gatekeepers. |\n\n---\n\n## System Roles\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban unifies human users, service accounts, and autonomous agents under 7 canonical principal tiers:\n\n1. **Guest** (`WORKSPACE_GUEST` / `PROJECT_GUEST`): Ephemeral or external collaborator. Confined strictly to explicitly shared objects with zero ambient project or workspace visibility.\n2. **Viewer** (`WORKSPACE_VIEWER` / `PROJECT_VIEWER`): Read-only stakeholder. Permitted to inspect unrestricted workspace or project assets, but cannot author or modify data.\n3. **Member** (`WORKSPACE_MEMBER` / `PROJECT_MEMBER`): Standard day-to-day engineer or contributor. Can author and manage issues, docs, stickies, and views in assigned projects.\n4. **Project Admin** (`PROJECT_ADMIN`): Lead for a specific project. Controls project configuration, workflow state transitions, WIP limits, project member bindings, and project trash.\n5. **Workspace Admin** (`WORKSPACE_ADMIN`): Organization administrator. Governs workspace settings, groups, user provisioning, retention policy, and workspace trash studio.\n6. **Server Admin** (`SERVER_ADMIN`): Root platform operator. Manages global server topology, multi-card authentication, air-gap flags, and cryptographic permanent purge.\n7. **Scoped MCP Agent (Service Principal):** Autonomous or assisted agent accessing `/mcp/agent`, `/mcp/docs`, or `/mcp/admin` bound to an API key or OAuth 2.0 PKCE token.\n\n---\n\n## Workspace-Level Roles\n\nWorkspace roles govern tenancy defaults, administrative delegation, and cross-project visibility:\n\n- **Workspace Admin:** Holds full administrative authority across all projects, custom fields, user groups, and workflows within the workspace. Enforces AAL2 step-up for user lifecycle mutations and trash restoration.\n- **Workspace Member:** Baseline contributor role assigned to standard enterprise users. Can create and participate in projects where granted explicit project membership.\n- **Workspace Viewer:** Auditing and stakeholder role with read-only visibility into workspace settings, public projects, and shared documentation.\n- **Workspace Guest:** Restricted access tier for external contractors and vendors. Has no ambient visibility into workspace member lists or project catalogs; visibility is granted exclusively through direct resource ACL grants.\n\nRole inheritance is strictly additive except where explicit DENY masks are applied. A user who is a Workspace Member can be elevated to Project Admin on specific projects without granting broader workspace administration privileges.\n\n---\n\n## Granular RBAC Policy Builder\n\nThe Granular RBAC Policy Builder (`/settings/workspace` -> **Roles & Permissions**) provides a narrative interface for authoring and managing custom role definitions with fine-grained capability sets.\n\n![Custom RBAC Policy Builder](images/slice1-custom-rbac-policy-builder.png)\n\n### Narrative Policy Configuration Header\n\nThe policy editor frames permission assignment as an intuitive narrative sentence:\n\n> **\"As a [ system admin | workspace admin | project admin ] I want [ \u25cf role x ] ... to have access to\"**\n\n- **Tier Scope Selector:** Pins the target scope of the role being defined (`system admin`, `workspace admin`, or `project admin`). Built-in roles belonging to higher tiers are locked against modification by lower-tier administrators.\n- **Role Selector & Creation Popover:** Allows administrators to select an existing custom role or click **Create Custom Role** to specify role name, slug, badge color, and description.\n- **Tri-State Checkboxes:** Permissions are toggled across three states:\n  - **Unchecked (\u25cb):** Inherits default permission behavior from lower tiers or defaults to Deny.\n  - **Checked (\u25cf):** Explicitly grants the capability.\n  - **Indeterminate / Deny:** Applies an explicit Deny mask that overrides all inherited permissions.\n\n### Step-by-Step Guide: Building Custom RBAC Roles\n\n1. **Open RBAC Studio:** Navigate to Workspace Settings and select **Roles & Permissions**.\n2. **Select Scope Tier:** In the narrative sentence header, select the target administrative scope (e.g., `workspace admin`).\n3. **Define Custom Role Identity:** Click the role pill, select **Create Custom Role**, and enter a descriptive **Role Name** (e.g., `Security Auditor`), lowercase alphanumeric **Slug** (e.g., `security-auditor`), and badge **Color** preset.\n4. **Configure Workspace Tier:** Toggle capabilities for member management, audit inspection, and integration configuration.\n5. **Configure Issue Tier:** Toggle capabilities for creating issues, transitioning workflow states, moving rank, linking, and managing item ACLs.\n6. **Configure Field Tier:** Toggle read and edit capabilities for standard and custom fields.\n7. **Save Policy:** Click **Save Changes**. The backend executes `POST /api/v1/admin/rbac/roles` or `PUT /api/v1/admin/rbac/roles/{role_id}`, validating caller AAL2 elevation and persisting the policy in `rbac_roles` and `rbac_role_permissions`.\n\n---\n\n## 30-Permission Granular Engine\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban implements 30 granular permission keys across three distinct operational tiers:\n\n### 1. Workspace Tier (8 Permissions)\n- `workspace:create` - Provision new tenant workspaces.\n- `workspace:edit_settings` - Modify workspace metadata, retention thresholds, and default roles.\n- `workspace:manage_members` - Invite, deactivate, and remove workspace members.\n- `workspace:manage_groups` - Create and manage principal groups and nested group hierarchies.\n- `workspace:create_role` - Author custom RBAC roles and modify role permission bitmasks.\n- `workspace:create_project` - Create new projects within the workspace.\n- `workspace:manage_trash` - Inspect soft-deleted workspace objects and restore items.\n- `workspace:manage_mcp_keys` - Mint, scope, and revoke MCP API tokens.\n\n### 2. Issue Tier (10 Permissions)\n- `issue:create` - Author new issues, tasks, and bugs.\n- `issue:view` - Read issue details, history, and metadata.\n- `issue:comment` - Post comments and replies on work items.\n- `issue:transition` - Move issues between workflow states.\n- `issue:move_rank` - Reorder issues within Kanban columns and backlogs.\n- `issue:link` - Create typed object links between issues, stickies, and docs.\n- `issue:copy` - Duplicate existing issues with selective metadata cloning.\n- `issue:archive` - Archive completed or stale issues outside active board views.\n- `issue:delete` - Soft-delete issues to the project trash bin.\n- `issue:manage_acl` - Share items with specific principals or set explicit Deny entries.\n\n### 3. Field Tier (12 Permissions)\n- `field:title:view` / `field:title:edit` - Inspect and modify issue titles.\n- `field:description:view` / `field:description:edit` - Inspect and author canonical markdown descriptions.\n- `field:assignee:view` / `field:assignee:edit` - Inspect and change issue assignment.\n- `field:priority:view` / `field:priority:edit` - Inspect and update issue priority tiers.\n- `field:estimate:view` / `field:estimate:edit` - Inspect and update story point estimates.\n- `field:custom:view` / `field:custom:edit` - Inspect and modify custom scripted and formula field values.\n\n---\n\n## Capability Bitmask and Deny Precedence\n\nTo guarantee high-performance authorization evaluation without recursive database queries, \ud83d\udc4dkanban compiles permissions into an authoritative 8-bit integer bitmask:\n\n```python\nclass Capability(IntFlag):\n    NONE = 0\n    VIEW = 1 << 0        # 1\n    COMMENT = 1 << 1     # 2\n    EDIT = 1 << 2        # 4\n    TRANSITION = 1 << 3  # 8\n    LINK = 1 << 4        # 16\n    SHARE = 1 << 5       # 32\n    ADMIN = 1 << 6       # 64\n    DELETE = 1 << 7      # 128\n    ALL = 0xFF           # 255\n```\n\n### Absolute DENY Precedence Rule\n\nWhen computing effective access for a user or agent across inherited groups and direct ACLs:\n\n$$\\text{Effective Capability} = (\\text{Inherited} \\cup \\text{Direct Allow}) \\setminus \\text{Direct Deny}$$\n\nIf any role, group, or explicit resource ACL specifies an explicit `DENY` mask for a capability, that capability is mathematically stripped (`allow & (~deny)`). An explicit `DENY` takes precedence over all administrative tiers below Server Administrator.\n\n---\n\n## Master Capability Matrix\n\n| Operational Capability | Guest | Viewer | Member | Project Admin | Workspace Admin | Server Admin | Scoped MCP Agent |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **Viewing Workspace-Public Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Viewing Private Project Objects** | \u25d0 (2) | \u25d0 (2) | \u25d0 (2) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 2) |\n| **Explicit ACL DENY Precedence** | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) |\n| **Authoring Issues, Stickies, and Docs** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Editing and Versioning Pages** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Managing Resource ACLs (Share / Revoke)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (4) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 4) |\n| **Project Studio and Workflow Management** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Custom Field and Script Definition** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (5) | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 5) |\n| **Soft-Trash Project Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (6) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 6) |\n| **Workspace Trash Studio Inspection** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (7) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1, 8) |\n| **Restoring Soft-Deleted Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (7) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1, 8) |\n| **Workspace Retention Policy (7 to 365 Days)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Automated Multi-Object Sweep (trash_purge)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (9) | \u25cb |\n| **2-Stage Permanent Purge (Cryptographic)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8, 10) | \u25cb |\n| **Local User Provisioning and Password Reset** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Role Bindings and Group Hierarchy CRUD** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (11) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Multi-Card Auth Studio and Passkey Config** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Minting Scoped MCP API Keys** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Immutable Audit Ledger (Inspection Only)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Tampering with Audit Ledger Records** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb (12) | \u25cb |\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Condition Notes\n\n1. **Token Scope Restriction:** Scoped MCP Agents can only exercise capabilities explicitly included in their minted token scopes (`read:issues`, `write:issues`, `read:docs`, `write:docs`, `admin`, etc.). Unscoped tools are rejected with `403 FORBIDDEN`.\n2. **Explicit Project Membership / ACL Share:** Guests and Viewers cannot see private project entities unless explicitly added to the project role bindings or granted a specific `ALLOW` entry in `resource_acl_entries`.\n3. **Absolute DENY Precedence:** If an explicit `DENY` entry exists for a principal on an object (or inherited group), effective capability bitmasks collapse immediately (`allow & (~deny)`). Even Workspace Admins cannot view or manage objects guarded by an explicit `DENY`.\n4. **Ownership Share Delegation:** Standard Members can only share objects they originally authored, provided project policy permits user-level ACL delegation.\n5. **Admin Approval Gate:** Custom fields and scripts can only be defined by administrators. Executing a script with Workspace or Server token escalation requires cryptographic approval from an administrator of that tier.\n6. **Author Deletion Scope:** Members may soft-delete their own drafts, comments, and unassigned stickies if granted DELETE capability mask. Project-wide item soft-deletion requires Project Admin.\n7. **Project Scope Isolation:** Project Admins in the Trash Studio can only view and restore items belonging to projects where they hold explicit `PROJECT_ADMIN` authority.\n8. **Fresh AAL2 Step-Up Requirement:** All administrative endpoints (`/api/v1/admin/*`, retention settings, user provisioning, trash operations, key minting) enforce `Depends(require_admin_aal2)`. The session must have verified MFA within the last 900 seconds (`aal2_verified_at <= 900s`).\n9. **Daemon Background Job Authority:** The trash purge runner executes with dedicated system worker identity and sweeps expired entities strictly past their per-workspace `trash_retention_days` threshold.\n10. **2-Stage Destructive Confirmation:** Permanent purge is exclusively gated to `SERVER_ADMIN` + fresh AAL2. It requires `POST /api/v1/admin/destructive:request` to compute blast radius and mint an ephemeral HMAC `confirmation_token` + `blast_hash`, followed by `POST /api/v1/admin/destructive:execute` with a mandatory human reason (10 to 500 characters).\n11. **Project-Level Role Delegation:** Project Admins may manage role bindings within their designated project only. They cannot elevate users to Workspace Admin or Server Admin.\n12. **Cryptographic Immutability:** Audit ledger tables (`activity_ledger`) have no `UPDATE` or `DELETE` grants for any database role (including `kanban_app` and `kanban_migrator`). Database triggers prevent tampering.\n\n---\n\n## Architectural Security Invariants\n\n- **Hostile Wire Invariant:** Every input is validated with strict Pydantic schemas and UTF-8 surrogate checks. Cleartext transmission of tokens is prohibited.\n- **Walled Component Garden:** Row-Level Security (`FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`) is always active on all database sessions. Dropping session authorization to unprivileged users is mandatory in application flows.\n- **Volatile State Sanitization:** Ephemeral tokens and secrets exist only in memory during execution and are erased immediately after verification.\n- **Supply Chain Paranoia:** Zero external cloud runtime dependencies for core authentication, authorization, or search.\n"
